{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf9MRS1orPbe7KTy7mco3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed. Summary of the fix in `bin/attavo`:\n\n- **`_merges_reachable`**: one `git log --merges --diff-merges=first-parent --name-only` call replaces the per-merge `git diff` loop in `merge_introducing_records`, which now takes an optional precomputed `merges` list.\n- **`commits_with_diffs`**: one `git log --diff-merges=first-parent --name-only` call per walked range replaces `commits_since` + a `git diff` per commit.\n- **`_record_blobs_at`**: one `git cat-file --batch` call replaces the per-record `git show` in the old `_record_at`, still spilling each blob to a temp file and reading it through `_load_record` so record-parsing stays the single site issue #60 requires.\n- `cmd_ledger` computes the merge list once and shares it across every item instead of recomputing it per item.\n\nVerified: ledger/doctor/stops/attest test suites pass (66 passed), the two spec fixtures pass manually (19 git processes for 6 items vs. the 60 ceiling; 4 vs 4 processes for 4-record vs 12-record items), and the two pre-existing `test_adapters.py` failures are unrelated (they exercise `adapters/claude-code/run`, untouched by this change)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":117334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":489},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"884efe91-ac12-4d2f-991f-d41420d3856c","uuid":"26784614-942d-44a8-b018-e748b6913d96","timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:48:04.426Z","request_id":"req_011Cf9MRRX33XUVYzo9Tv3xo"}
